{
  "change_id": "mock-2297-control",
  "requirement_id": "REQ-2297",
  "requirement_title": "Add ExcludeFromCodeCoverage attribute to generated code.",
  "requirement_text": "# REQ-2297: Add ExcludeFromCodeCoverage attribute to generated code.\n\nSource: https://github.com/MessagePack-CSharp/MessagePack-CSharp/issues/2297\nType: feature\n\n## Requirement\n\nMessagePack generated code is not decorated with the `ExcludeFromCodeCoverage` attribute. Because it is very hard to write good coverage for generated MessagePack code, it may skew coverage numbers, especially on large projects with a lot of generated code.\n\nSolution requested: \"I would like all generated code to be decorated with ExcludeFromCodeCoverage attribute.  I do not feel like a setting is needed, but setting would be fine to have too.\"\n\nAlternatives considered by the author: none; \"it is close to impossible to write good coverage for generated code as it covers many edge cases.\"\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- All generated code is decorated with `ExcludeFromCodeCoverage`.\n- No new setting or option is required to get the attribute. (\"I do not feel like a setting is needed\")\n- An opt-out setting would be acceptable but is optional. (\"setting would be fine to have too\")\n- The generated code still compiles on every supported target framework (the attribute must exist there or be conditionally emitted). (derived)\n- Existing verified generator snapshots are updated to include the attribute. (derived)\n\n## Notes from discussion\n\n- b-kurczynski-dl suggests a coverage-tool workaround instead: exclude `obj\\\\.*\\.g\\.cs$` in the `dotnet-coverage` settings XML.\n- armadavalor offers a PR: add `[global::System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis.ExcludeFromCodeCoverage]` (and possibly `GeneratedCode`) to the types emitted by the templates under `src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/Transforms/` (formatters, string-key formatters, enum/union formatters, resolvers), update the verified snapshots, no setting. Asks AArnott whether he would accept it or prefer to point users at coverage-tool configuration. No maintainer reply in the thread.\n- Ambiguity driver: scope (all generated types vs formatters only) and setting (unconditional vs opt-out) are both open.",
  "run_ts": "20261114T071212Z",
